        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=2$",
          "worked": "Let $y=2^x$, so $y>0$ and $2^{2x}=y^2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y^2-y-12&=0\\\\(y-4)(y+3)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nThe roots are $4$ and $-3$. Since $y>0$, use $y=4$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2^x&=4=2^2\\\\x&=2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
