        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=2$",
          "worked": "Let $y=3^x$, so $y>0$ and $3^{2x}=y^2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y^2-8y-9&=0\\\\(y-9)(y+1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nThe roots are $9$ and $-1$. Since $y>0$, use $y=9$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3^x&=9=3^2\\\\x&=2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-p2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$3^{2x}-12\\times 3^x+27=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=1$ or $x=2$",
          "worked": "Let $y=3^x$, so $3^{2x}=y^2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y^2-12y+27&=0\\\\(y-3)(y-9)&=0\\\\y&=3\\text{ or }9\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute back.\n$$\\begin{align*}3^x&=3\\text{ or }9=3^2\\\\x&=1\\text{ or }2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-p2-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$3\\times 9^x-3^{x+1}-18=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=1$",
          "worked": "Let $y=3^x$, so $y>0$, $9^x=(3^x)^2=y^2$ and $3^{x+1}=3y$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3y^2-3y-18&=0\\\\y^2-y-6&=0\\\\(y-3)(y+2)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nThe roots are $3$ and $-2$. Since $y>0$, use $y=3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3^x&=3\\\\x&=1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-p2-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$(x^2+x)^2-8(x^2+x)+12=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-3,-2,1,2$\n\nSubstitute $y=x^2+x$, then solve for $x$ at each root of the quadratic in $y$.",
          "worked": "Let $y=x^2+x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y^2-8y+12&=0\\\\(y-2)(y-6)&=0\\\\y&=2\\text{ or }6\\end{align*}$$\nFor $y=2$,\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+x&=2\\\\x^2+x-2&=0\\\\(x+2)(x-1)&=0\\\\x&=-2\\text{ or }1\\end{align*}$$\nFor $y=6$,\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+x&=6\\\\x^2+x-6&=0\\\\(x+3)(x-2)&=0\\\\x&=-3\\text{ or }2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
